# 📖 Overview

The **Bank Management System** is a console-based application that simulates essential banking operations through a structured and modular C++ implementation.

The system allows authorized employees to manage clients, perform banking transactions, and administer system users while enforcing **Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)** through binary permissions.

This project was developed to strengthen practical knowledge of:

- Modular Programming
- File Handling
- Structured Programming
- Data Persistence
- Bitwise Operations
- Software Design Principles

---

# ✨ Features

## 🔑 Authentication

- Secure login system
- Username & password authentication
- Session-based access

---

## 🛡️ Role-Based Access Control

- Binary (bitwise) permission system
- Feature-level authorization
- Administrator privileges
- Access denied protection

---

## 👥 Client Management

✔ List Clients

✔ Add New Client

✔ Update Client Information

✔ Delete Client

✔ Find Client

---

## 💰 Transactions

✔ Deposit Money

✔ Withdraw Money

✔ Balance Validation

✔ View Client Balances

✔ Calculate Total Bank Balance

---

## 👨‍💼 User Management

Only users with the **Manage Users** permission can access this module.

✔ List Users

✔ Add Users

✔ Update Users

✔ Delete Users

✔ Find Users

✔ Assign Permissions

---

## 💾 Data Persistence

- Client records stored in text files
- User records stored separately
- Automatic loading at startup
- Automatic saving after every operation

